; First instruction starts observed (in the runs named above) that the removal
; of the entries below the segment starts left undecoded.
code S066A:0006

; The battle: CODE:013A calls it, the map is drawn and the keys are compared
; in it (read from the code; its S and E branches were followed for the
; names below).
; game_loop is the program's main (argc, argv): /a or /b on the command
; line, the allocation of 445C0h bytes, the screen, the menu and the loads
; of a battle come before the loop (read in part, see docs/HANDOFF.md).
name S066A:000D game_loop
; Saving: in a run, a click (the F1 prompt), D and a digit wrote the file
; 03.DAT into the state folder. The D key (entry 1Ah of the key table) is
; compared at S066A:3FA7, reached while the other side's state byte is 5 and
; the key is not F1; the routine's result is the number of the text shown.
name S1273:0005 save_game
; Loading: called at the start of game_loop when bit 200h of S331F:4CA4 is
; set; a run that chose MISC, LOAD and the digit continued the saved battle.
; That this routine reads the file is read from its code (it calls
; file_open), not shown by a breakpoint.
name S1273:0399 load_game

